<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Neugablonz</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Neugablonz is a district of Kaufbeuren in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bavaria">Bavaria</a> founded after 1945 by German refugees expelled from Gablonz, now <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jablonec-nad-nisou">Jablonec nad Nisou</a>, in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bohemia">Bohemia</a>. Built on the site of a former explosives factory, it revived the glass and costume-jewellery industry of its founders' home town and became one of the largest settlements of expellees in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a>.</p></div>
